<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees Sept CPI at 4.1 yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees Sept CPI at 4.1 yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its September consumer price index stood at 0.3 percent month-on-month and 4.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Venice's inflation rate was flat and 4.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3   (0.0)     4.1  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2  (-0.4)     3.9  (5.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.3   (0.0)     4.6  (5.1)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.4   (0.5)     2.8  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.5)     5.0  (5.2)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.3   (0.0)     1.1  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.9   (0.2)     4.1  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.2  (-0.2)     2.0  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0  (-0.4)     3.1  (5.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.9  (-0.1)     9.2  (9.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1  (-0.1)     1.7  (1.9)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
</text>
